# FREEZE_BINDING — the two-way digest binding for the M5 campaign freeze
# and its machine-readable companion.
#
# WHAT THIS IS
#   `docs/design/M5_CAMPAIGN_FREEZE_2026-08-27.md` (the freeze, "D") and
#   `benchmarks/m5-v1/campaign.yaml` (the companion, "Y") each pin the
#   other's identity. Y already carries D's hash directly (its own
#   `freeze_sha256` field). D cannot carry Y's hash directly without
#   creating a self-referential fixpoint — see Addendum 3 in the freeze
#   document for the full account of why that specific idea doesn't work.
#   This file exists to carry the missing half instead: it is written
#   LAST, after both D and Y are final, and it depends on both of them;
#   neither of them depends on it, so there is no cycle.
#
# WHAT scripts/bench_m5.py CHECKS, AT EVERY RUN, BEFORE TOUCHING A STORE
#   (a) sha256(D) == campaign.yaml's own `freeze_sha256` field
#       — catches the FREEZE DOCUMENT drifting or being tampered.
#   (b) sha256(Y) == this file's `campaign_yaml_sha256` line below
#       — catches THE COMPANION (any frozen parameter inside it — a gate
#         threshold, a window fraction, a floor) drifting or being
#         tampered, INCLUDING a copy of campaign.yaml passed via
#         --campaign-yaml that a legitimate `freeze_sha256` field was
#         copied into verbatim but some OTHER line was edited. This is
#         the exact gap coordinator re-verification found: a `sed` of
#         R-13's bar (10.0 -> 9.9) leaves `freeze_sha256` untouched and
#         only (b) catches it.
#   A mismatch on either refuses the run outright, by name, before any
#   store is opened or any record is written.
#
# HOW TO REGENERATE (only ever as part of a ratified, dated addendum —
# never casually; this file's own bytes are not append-only the way the
# freeze document's are, but a change to it outside a dated addendum
# process is itself a post-hoc revision under §H and must say so)
#   1. Finalize the freeze document (with its new addendum, if any).
#   2. sha256 it; write that value into campaign.yaml's `freeze_sha256`.
#   3. Finalize campaign.yaml (both edits done).
#   4. sha256 IT; write that value into this file's `campaign_yaml_sha256`.
#   5. sha256 the freeze document again to confirm step 2's value is still
#      correct (it is, since this file was written after the freeze
#      document and never fed back into it) and record it below too, for
#      a reader auditing this file without re-deriving from campaign.yaml.

